### 2c. Opaque KDF Dependency

`kdf::hkdf_to_slice` is configured opaque in `aeneas-config.yml`
(line 43, [issue #104](https://github.com/Beneficial-AI-Foundation/SparsePostQuantumRatchet-verify/issues/104))
and appears as an axiom in `SrcTranslated/FunsExternal.lean`. It is not
a chain function, but F16 (`next_key_internal`), F22 (`Chain::new`) and
F23 (`add_epoch`) call it directly, so their spec theorems can only be
stated *relative to* the abstract KDF (length/shape postconditions and
`ctr` update laws), not about concrete key bytes.

Note that unlike the polynomial layer, `KeyHistory::gc` and
`KeyHistory::get` are marked `#[hax_lib::opaque]` **for hax only**
(slice ordering / `step_by` model); Aeneas *does* extract their bodies
(`gc_loop`, `get_loop`), so they remain fully verifiable here.

