## 5. Extraction Blockers and Tweaks

Unlike the polynomial layer, `src/chain.rs` extraction is clean:
**every function in `chain_functions.txt` (minus feature-gated / test
items) has a typed Lean body in `SrcTranslated/Funs.lean`** — including
`gc`, `get` and `into_pb`/`from_pb`, which are `#[hax_lib::opaque]`
only for the hax backend, not for Aeneas.

Chain-related `aeneas-config.yml` tweaks (fixes, not blockers):

| Tweak | Effect |
|-------|--------|
| `tweaks` (lines 95–104) | Renames the local variable `chain` to `chain'` in `spqr::send` because it shadows the module namespace `chain.Chain` ([issue #101](https://github.com/Beneficial-AI-Foundation/SparsePostQuantumRatchet-verify/issues/101)); fixes `chain.Chain.send_key` call sites. |
| `tweaks` (lines 106–115) | Same shadowing rename in `spqr::recv`, fixing `chain.Chain.into_pb` / `chain.Chain.recv_key` call sites. |
| `opaque` (line 43) | `spqr::kdf::hkdf_to_slice` — opaque axiom in `SrcTranslated/FunsExternal.lean` (issue #104); constrains F16, F22, F23 to KDF-relative specs. |

Prost-derived `Message` instance bodies for the chain protobufs are
`sorry` in `SrcTranslated/Funs.lean` (lines 4326, 4386, 4410, 4467, see
[issue #102](https://github.com/Beneficial-AI-Foundation/SparsePostQuantumRatchet-verify/issues/102)),
but these are protobuf wire-format scaffolding and are **not** on the
chain verification path.

